const items = [
    {
        q: "Who must comply with e-invoicing in Malaysia?",
        a: "All businesses carrying on business in Malaysia, phased in by annual turnover from 1 August 2024. From 1 September 2026, businesses with turnover below RM3 million are exempt if they meet LHDN's criteria. The exemption doesn't apply if a shareholder, holding company, or related company has turnover of RM3 million or more.",
    },
    {
        q: "What are the implementation phases?",
        a: "Phase 1 (above RM100 million) from 1 August 2024; Phase 2 (RM25 million to RM100 million) from 1 January 2025; Phase 3 (RM5 million to RM25 million) from 1 July 2025; and Phase 4 (up to RM5 million, unless exempt) from 1 January 2026, with relaxation until 31 December 2027.",
    },
    {
        q: "What is MyInvois?",
        a: "LHDN's e-invoicing system. Businesses submit each e-invoice to MyInvois through the portal or an API, and MyInvois validates it in near real time and returns a unique ID. After that, the issuer generates the QR code.",
    },
    {
        q: "Can I still issue consolidated e-invoices?",
        a: "Yes, for B2C sales where the buyer doesn't ask for an e-invoice, submitted within 7 days of month-end. During the relaxation period, eligible businesses can consolidate other transactions too. Outside it, any single transaction above RM10,000 needs its own e-invoice.",
    },
    {
        q: "What is a self-billed e-invoice?",
        a: "An e-invoice that the buyer issues instead of the supplier, for cases like imports from foreign suppliers, agent commissions and interest payments.",
    },
    {
        q: "What are the penalties for non-compliance?",
        a: "Failing to issue an e-invoice is an offence under Section 120(1)(d) of the Income Tax Act 1967, with a fine of RM200 to RM20,000, up to six months' imprisonment, or both, for each offence.",
    },
    {
        q: "How do I choose the right e-invoicing software for Malaysia?",
        a: "Look for proven MyInvois volumes, integration with your ERP and POS, validation before submission, monthly reconciliation with LHDN data, self-billing and B2C consolidation, fast handling of guideline changes and local support. MDEC accreditation is a useful signal.",
    },
];
